 {r}←parms ReportPackageProblems report;rows;markers;buff;plural;elsewhere
⍝ Prints whatever the check for later versions turned up that is not a later version.\\
⍝ `report` is what `CheckTatinFoldersForLaterVersions` collected: one matrix per install folder,
⍝ with the columns Tatin's `CheckForLaterVersion` defines.\\
⍝ Three things are worth saying, and none of them is an offer to update:
⍝ * A package whose [;2] carries one of Tatin's "<<< ... >>>" markers. "Not available any more"
⍝   is the one that matters: nobody can install that version again, so the project cannot be set
⍝   up from scratch any more, and the sooner that is known the better.
⍝ * A package the very same version of which is hosted by a Registry other than the one it was
⍝   installed from: [;2] repeats [;1], yet [;5] names a Registry. That is what a package looks
⍝   like that was installed from a local Registry before being published. Re-installing it
⍝   changes no version, it only corrects the URL the build list records.
⍝ * Packages that did not come from tatin.dev. This used to be said only when no later version
⍝   was found for anything, which is exactly when nobody is looking.
 r←0
 :If 0<≢report
     rows←⊃⍪/report
     :If 0<≢markers←('<'=⊃¨rows[;2])⌿rows
         (1 parms.batch)PrintToSession'These installed packages need attention:'
         (1 parms.batch)PrintToSession↓⎕FMT markers[;1 2]
     :EndIf
     :If 0<≢elsewhere←(IsAvailableElsewhere rows)⌿rows
         (1 parms.batch)PrintToSession'The very same version of these packages is available from another Registry:'
         (1 parms.batch)PrintToSession↓⎕FMT elsewhere[;1 3],(((≢elsewhere),1)⍴⊂' ==> '),elsewhere[;,5]
     :EndIf
     :If 0<≢buff←(⊂'https://tatin.dev/')~⍨rows[;3]
         plural←1<≢buff
         (1 parms.batch)PrintToSession plural{'Note that ',(⍕≢⍵),' package',(⍺/'s'),((1+⍺)⊃' was' ' were'),' loaded from ',⊃{⍺,',',⍵}/∪⍵}buff
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
